---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import DddMapper from '../components/mapper/DddMapper.tsx';
import { archPortalUrl, baPortalUrl, eventStormerUrl } from '../lib/links';

// Server-rendered: the footer resolves the neighbouring components' addresses
// from the environment, and those are configuration that has to be read per
// request rather than baked into the image at build time.
const portal = baPortalUrl();
const stormer = eventStormerUrl();
const arch = archPortalUrl();
---

<Layout
	title="DDD mapper — ba-hub"
	description="Who depends on whom, and on whose terms. A context map as text and as a graph: domains, subdomains and the bounded contexts that serve them, with every relationship tagged by the strategic pattern that governs it."
>
	<main id="main" class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[110rem] px-6 py-10">
		<header class="mb-8">
			{/*
				Three levels, and each answers a different question: the eyebrow says
				what this page is, the heading says why the artefact exists, and the
				paragraph says why at length. The heading used to say "the context
				map, and the text it is made of", which is how the tool works rather
				than what it is for — true, and no reason to draw one.
			*/}
			<p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.16em] text-ink-muted uppercase dark:text-slate-400">
				ba-hub · ddd mapper · context map
			</p>
			<h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">Who depends on whom, and on whose terms</h1>
			<p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted dark:text-slate-400">
				The estate seen whole: the domains the business is in, the subdomains they divide into,
				and the bounded contexts that serve them — with every relationship between contexts
				tagged by the pattern that governs it.
			</p>
		</header>

		<DddMapper client:only="react" />

		<noscript>
			<div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-6 dark:border-slate-700">
				<h2 class="font-semibold">The mapper needs JavaScript</h2>
				<p class="mt-2 max-w-prose text-ink-muted dark:text-slate-400">
					A graph is direct manipulation, which is not something a page can do without
					scripting. The file format is plain text and is documented on
					<a class="font-semibold text-brand underline" href="/dsl" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the format page</a>, which
					needs none.
				</p>
			</div>
		</noscript>

		<footer
			class="mt-10 border-t border-slate-200 pt-6 text-sm text-ink-muted dark:border-slate-700 dark:text-slate-400"
		>
			<p>
				Nothing here is stored on the server — the mapper keeps a copy in this browser, and that
				copy goes no further. The <code>.ddd</code> file you export is the context map. The practice is
				written up in the <a class="font-semibold text-brand underline" href={portal} target="_blank" rel="noopener">business
				analysis hub</a>; the contexts on a map are usually found first on a wall in
				the <a class="font-semibold text-brand underline" href={stormer} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Event Stormer</a>, and
				what they get realised as lives in
				the <a class="font-semibold text-brand underline" href={arch} target="_blank" rel="noopener">architecture hub</a>.
				The <a class="font-semibold text-brand underline" href="/dsl" target="_blank" rel="noopener">format is documented</a>.
			</p>
		</footer>
	</main>
</Layout>
